1
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:03,000
=Ren Yu=

2
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,160
(Adapted from Lei Mi's novel Ren Yu)

3
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:08,160
=Episode 6=

4
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,520
Go away!

5
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,199
Stab me! Come on!

6
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:11,879
Stay back!

7
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,479
All of you, stay back!

8
00:03:13,599 --> 00:03:14,560
What are you doing?

9
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:31,960
Are you crazy?

10
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:38,680
Tell the principal.

11
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:39,879
Go tell him.

12
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:41,840
Go!

13
00:03:42,759 --> 00:03:43,560
Mr. Zhou.

14
00:03:44,039 --> 00:03:45,879
School's already out.

15
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,759
You're a part-time teacher.

16
00:03:47,759 --> 00:03:48,840
You can't boss us around.

17
00:03:55,599 --> 00:03:56,199
Fair point.

18
00:03:57,639 --> 00:03:59,039
Then let's settle this

19
00:03:59,080 --> 00:03:59,800
like adults.

20
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:13,919
The camera.

21
00:04:14,719 --> 00:04:15,759
I forgot to turn it off.

22
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:17,720
This tape

23
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:21,360
caught everything that happened here.

24
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,399
Take it to the cops.

25
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,839
Tell them your story.

26
00:04:27,199 --> 00:04:27,800
What do we do?

27
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,079
What now?

28
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,240
Sorry, Mr. Zhou.

29
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:45,759
Mr. Zhou.

30
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
We were wrong.

31
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,439
We'll never do it again.

32
00:05:02,399 --> 00:05:03,160
This tape

33
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:04,920
will stay somewhere safe.

34
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:08,040
Don't ever bully anyone again.

35
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:19,720
Let's go.

36
00:05:32,439 --> 00:05:33,600
Thank you, Mr. Zhou.

37
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:40,839
Don't thank me.

38
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,959
Thank Yang Le.

39
00:05:46,199 --> 00:05:47,839
He saw you here with them

40
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:49,839
and feared for you,

41
00:05:50,519 --> 00:05:51,720
so he sent me to check on you.

42
00:06:39,199 --> 00:06:39,720
Jiang Ting.

43
00:06:41,079 --> 00:06:43,639
Did Ma Na give you any trouble?

44
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,480
Today,

45
00:06:48,319 --> 00:06:50,480
I heard you ask Mr. Zhou about Su Lin.

46
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,120
Su Lin dropped out.

47
00:06:52,839 --> 00:06:54,319
Do you know why?

48
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,040
Was it because of Ma Na?

49
00:07:00,319 --> 00:07:01,279
Thanks for today.

50
00:07:02,319 --> 00:07:04,519
But I don't know about Su Lin.

51
00:07:05,279 --> 00:07:05,800
Jiang Ting.

52
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:06,399
Jiang Ting.

53
00:07:06,639 --> 00:07:07,839
I think Su Lin dropped out

54
00:07:07,839 --> 00:07:08,600
because of Ma Na.

55
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:09,360
I truly don't know.

56
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:09,920
Listen to me.

57
00:07:09,959 --> 00:07:10,519
Let go first.

58
00:07:10,519 --> 00:07:11,519
We can't let Ma Na go on.

59
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:12,199
- Jeez.
- Ting!

60
00:07:12,959 --> 00:07:13,720
Why grab her?

61
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,680
What is this?

62
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,839
He didn't do anything.

63
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,399
I'm asking you.

64
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,279
What are you doing?

65
00:07:18,519 --> 00:07:19,000
Ma'am.

66
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:20,199
He really did nothing.

67
00:07:20,199 --> 00:07:20,959
Wait here.

68
00:07:23,759 --> 00:07:24,319
Your name?

69
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,519
What class?

70
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,240
Sorry, ma'am.

71
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:30,120
Jiang Ting.

72
00:07:30,319 --> 00:07:30,839
Ting.

73
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:31,920
Hold it!

74
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,040
Ting! Ting!

75
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,480
Wait for me, Ting!

76
00:07:36,319 --> 00:07:37,040
Are you okay?

77
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:38,920
I'm fine.

78
00:07:39,519 --> 00:07:40,560
He didn't hurt you, right?

79
00:07:41,759 --> 00:07:42,680
He didn't.

80
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,040
I saw him yank you hard.

81
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:45,879
Does it hurt?

82
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:23,840
(Chaobei Vocational High School)

83
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:34,879
April 10.

84
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,159
The last person to see Yang Xinqian

85
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,960
was a friend from Chunfeng Orphanage.

86
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,799
They shopped at Xiangyun Market.

87
00:08:42,399 --> 00:08:43,240
They finished

88
00:08:43,639 --> 00:08:44,720
around 10:00 a.m.

89
00:08:45,159 --> 00:08:47,399
That day, she planned to meet a friend

90
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,639
for lunch on Liutiaohu East Road.

91
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:51,960
But she never showed.

92
00:08:52,559 --> 00:08:53,399
She never came back.

93
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,399
The poor girl.

94
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:56,720
Apparently,

95
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,559
she went there to borrow money.

96
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:01,120
She was really struggling.

97
00:09:01,799 --> 00:09:02,279
Yeah.

98
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,039
When I interviewed people there,

99
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:05,879
I spoke with

100
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,639
some of her old roommates.

101
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,840
They said when Yang Xinqian

102
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,080
(Central Blood Bank)
was poor,

103
00:09:11,279 --> 00:09:12,799
she sold blood there for cash.

104
00:09:13,039 --> 00:09:13,679
Sold blood?

105
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,639
Yes, sold blood.

106
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,879
Near Du Yuan's home,

107
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:23,679
isn't there a blood bank?

108
00:09:24,279 --> 00:09:24,960
The connection.

109
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,240
Low-income people.

110
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,120
The city's donor records

111
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,840
for the last two years are all here.

112
00:09:33,279 --> 00:09:34,159
Every shelf

113
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,639
is labeled with exact dates.

114
00:09:36,039 --> 00:09:36,879
Just use

115
00:09:36,879 --> 00:09:38,000
the date index to search.

116
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:38,639
It's easy.

117
00:09:39,039 --> 00:09:39,679
Thanks.

118
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:40,960
Carry on.

119
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,960
Let's contact Captain Wang

120
00:09:49,279 --> 00:09:50,080
and ask for backup.

121
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,000
Good idea.

122
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:56,799
I already

123
00:09:56,879 --> 00:09:59,240
suspected the killer had a record.

124
00:09:59,679 --> 00:10:01,759
I talked to old contacts just released.

125
00:10:01,759 --> 00:10:02,360
They told me

126
00:10:03,279 --> 00:10:03,879
that people

127
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,679
who hit rock bottom

128
00:10:05,759 --> 00:10:06,519
all come here.

129
00:10:06,759 --> 00:10:07,320
Blood bank?

130
00:10:07,919 --> 00:10:08,399
Right.

131
00:10:09,399 --> 00:10:10,159
They also lack

132
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:11,799
steady work or income.

133
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,799
When they can't get by,

134
00:10:14,039 --> 00:10:16,039
they donate blood for a stipend.

135
00:10:16,919 --> 00:10:18,679
I already checked the first two places.

136
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,080
The blood bank was last.

137
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,159
So the killer's income

138
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,120
is low and unstable.

139
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:26,360
He donates blood here now and then,

140
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:29,320
then targets other donors,

141
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,080
like Xinqian,

142
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:32,080
and Du Yuan, who lived nearby.

143
00:10:32,519 --> 00:10:33,919
It's possible.

144
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,639
If this theory is right,

145
00:10:35,799 --> 00:10:37,120
his donation record

146
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,480
is probably here.

147
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:39,840
Search.

148
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,000
Remember,

149
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,399
the killer is confirmed type A.

150
00:11:46,399 --> 00:11:47,639
(The water tower is haunted.)

151
00:11:48,159 --> 00:11:49,080
(Everyone is afraid.)

152
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:50,879
(I used to be too.)

153
00:11:53,679 --> 00:11:55,120
(But once I climbed it,)

154
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,559
(I knew there was nothing to fear.)

155
00:11:58,559 --> 00:11:59,639
(It even suits me.)

156
00:12:03,879 --> 00:12:04,600
(Open.)

157
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:06,440
(Quiet.)

158
00:12:07,679 --> 00:12:09,200
(Only the wind speaks to me.)

159
00:12:10,799 --> 00:12:12,000
(From the water tower,)

160
00:12:13,039 --> 00:12:14,600
(I can see far into the distance.)

161
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:19,200
(I can see beyond this city.)

162
00:12:21,039 --> 00:12:24,480
(One day, I'll go there.)

163
00:12:37,759 --> 00:12:40,919
Where is that girl hiding?

164
00:12:41,679 --> 00:12:44,200
She's making me search everywhere.

165
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,960
Please be okay.

166
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,500
(Sealed)

167
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,039
Anyone there?

168
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,120
Can you hear me?

169
00:13:53,159 --> 00:13:54,480
Is anyone there?

170
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,480
Anyone?

171
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:58,879
Someone's trapped down here!

172
00:13:59,559 --> 00:14:01,600
Someone's trapped down here!

173
00:14:02,159 --> 00:14:03,480
Help!

174
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:12,919
Is anyone there?

175
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,919
Someone help me!

176
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:24,879
You're really

177
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:25,840
brave, aren't you?

178
00:14:26,039 --> 00:14:26,679
Come on. Move!

179
00:14:26,879 --> 00:14:27,639
It's haunted here.

180
00:14:27,679 --> 00:14:28,480
Hurry!

181
00:14:28,519 --> 00:14:30,039
Don't stay here another second.

182
00:14:30,159 --> 00:14:30,480
Go!

183
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:33,039
Someone's trapped down here!

184
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,000
Can you hear me?

185
00:14:36,039 --> 00:14:37,559
Can you hear me?

186
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:09,759
I'm exhausted.

187
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,399
I'm beat.

188
00:15:12,879 --> 00:15:14,000
Thanks, Captain Li.

189
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,759
Don't you know this place is haunted?

190
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:18,200
Why'd you come

191
00:15:18,279 --> 00:15:19,039
here at midnight?

192
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:20,000
I was just...

193
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:23,840
Why'd you come

194
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:24,960
here at midnight?

195
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,000
Don't tell me...

196
00:15:29,159 --> 00:15:30,600
I saved you, you know.

197
00:15:30,919 --> 00:15:31,799
Ingrate.

198
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:34,879
What did you see?

199
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,399
Any ghosts?

200
00:15:37,759 --> 00:15:38,159
Yes.

201
00:15:38,759 --> 00:15:39,399
It's haunted.

202
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,039
You're all ghosts.

203
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:56,120
Did you wet your pants or not?

204
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,399
Cat got your tongue? Answer me.

205
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,320
Speak up!

206
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:05,840
Good.

207
00:16:06,879 --> 00:16:09,120
Who'll wash your clothes back home?

208
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,120
Why are you here?

209
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,120
Why are you here?

210
00:16:25,879 --> 00:16:27,240
You're nearby. Why not eat at home?

211
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,200
Mr. Gu, soup dumplings.

212
00:16:29,559 --> 00:16:29,960
One tray.

213
00:16:30,639 --> 00:16:30,879
Okay.

214
00:16:30,879 --> 00:16:32,360
I just got off. I stopped for a bite.

215
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,840
Mom would scold me if I went home.

216
00:16:34,519 --> 00:16:35,120
So thoughtful.

217
00:16:36,639 --> 00:16:37,799
Afraid she'll worry?

218
00:16:39,679 --> 00:16:40,240
Eat first.

219
00:16:41,519 --> 00:16:42,600
Stuck on the case?

220
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:43,680
Yeah.

221
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,200
We've narrowed down the group,

222
00:16:49,679 --> 00:16:51,080
but nothing points to anyone.

223
00:16:51,679 --> 00:16:52,399
The trail's cold.

224
00:16:53,559 --> 00:16:55,159
We have this many suspects,

225
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,200
but can't narrow it any further.

226
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,480
That's the problem.

227
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:00,480
I once worked a case.

228
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:02,840
In winter, people stored cabbage

229
00:17:02,919 --> 00:17:04,039
in the hallways.

230
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,680
One elderly woman

231
00:17:06,519 --> 00:17:08,720
lost one cabbage every day.

232
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,279
She filed a report

233
00:17:11,599 --> 00:17:12,519
to catch the thief.

234
00:17:13,039 --> 00:17:14,279
Guess who it was.

235
00:17:15,119 --> 00:17:15,759
A neighbor?

236
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,880
A stray dog.

237
00:17:19,319 --> 00:17:21,559
The hallway was warm in winter,

238
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:24,160
and the dog couldn't find food.

239
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:27,000
It came by every night

240
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,920
and carried off one cabbage.

241
00:17:31,839 --> 00:17:32,799
How'd you crack it?

242
00:17:33,319 --> 00:17:34,319
At first,

243
00:17:34,359 --> 00:17:36,400
I kept wondering what kind of person

244
00:17:37,279 --> 00:17:38,519
would steal cabbage.

245
00:17:39,039 --> 00:17:40,359
One head a day.

246
00:17:40,839 --> 00:17:42,480
Why not take several at once?

247
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:44,119
Then I noticed

248
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,799
that my neighbor had a dog

249
00:17:47,319 --> 00:17:48,759
that loved cabbage.

250
00:17:49,519 --> 00:17:50,359
Then it clicked.

251
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,920
I'd boxed in my own thinking.

252
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,079
Tunnel vision.

253
00:17:54,519 --> 00:17:55,240
So sometimes,

254
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,480
you must break away.

255
00:17:57,759 --> 00:17:59,519
View the case from the outside.

256
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,920
You can even imagine you're a dog

257
00:18:02,799 --> 00:18:04,640
and see things from its perspective.

258
00:18:05,799 --> 00:18:07,480
That's another line of inquiry.

259
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:08,559
Me?

260
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:09,799
A police dog.

261
00:18:11,759 --> 00:18:13,160
Sure. Pretty cool.

262
00:18:15,519 --> 00:18:17,200
Two baskets of buns, please.

263
00:18:17,599 --> 00:18:18,000
Coming up.

264
00:18:18,039 --> 00:18:19,240
To go, please.

265
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:20,720
For your mom?

266
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,440
For the bureau.

267
00:18:22,799 --> 00:18:24,279
They haven't eaten yet.

268
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,200
A few years ago,

269
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:29,519
our city

270
00:18:29,799 --> 00:18:31,480
caught a serial killer.

271
00:18:31,559 --> 00:18:32,279
I want to meet him

272
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:34,519
and learn how he thought.

273
00:18:39,079 --> 00:18:40,279
The serial killer?

274
00:18:41,359 --> 00:18:42,240
You can't just visit.

275
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:44,039
Don't you know the procedure?

276
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:46,000
You act on every whim.

277
00:18:46,799 --> 00:18:48,400
First, go through all 3,000 files.

278
00:18:48,839 --> 00:18:49,480
Every one.

279
00:19:03,599 --> 00:19:04,200
Being punished?

280
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,119
What for?

281
00:19:13,519 --> 00:19:14,279
An essay?

282
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:17,240
Read it to me.

283
00:19:19,559 --> 00:19:21,759
My dad has a terrible temper.

284
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,559
He always yells at Mom,

285
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:25,039
my sister, and me.

286
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,240
Mom and my sister

287
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,400
are always too scared to speak.

288
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,359
He's always scolding me too,

289
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:33,920
and won't let me go out.

290
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,160
Haven't you shamed us enough?

291
00:19:35,839 --> 00:19:36,680
Get back inside!

292
00:19:39,839 --> 00:19:40,440
My apologies.

293
00:19:41,039 --> 00:19:41,599
Su.

294
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,839
He just started school.

295
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:45,519
Lots of homework.

296
00:19:46,119 --> 00:19:47,119
Maybe he's not used to it

297
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:48,480
He'll adjust.

298
00:19:49,039 --> 00:19:50,559
I never knew it was such a hassle.

299
00:19:50,839 --> 00:19:52,720
It's chaos every day.

300
00:19:53,039 --> 00:19:54,720
His sister used to teach him.

301
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:55,839
Right?

302
00:19:57,559 --> 00:19:58,480
Isn't she back yet?

303
00:19:59,380 --> 00:19:59,900
Oh.

304
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,200
She went away for school.

305
00:20:04,759 --> 00:20:06,720
His registration is settled?

306
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:08,440
He couldn't attend otherwise.

307
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:10,759
See you.

308
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:12,039
How'd you do it?

309
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,480
I paid the fine.

310
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:21,200
Why do you ask?

311
00:20:23,559 --> 00:20:24,559
I have a friend

312
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:26,640
in the same situation.

313
00:20:28,559 --> 00:20:29,279
I'm asking for him.

314
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:34,039
There wasn't any other way.

315
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:37,640
I recently landed a big job

316
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:38,880
and saved some money.

317
00:20:39,519 --> 00:20:41,279
I just paid the overdue fine.

318
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:43,440
See you.

319
00:21:22,119 --> 00:21:22,880
Careful.

320
00:21:27,039 --> 00:21:28,319
Mom, you're still up?

321
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:31,640
Waiting for you.

322
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:32,800
Oh.

323
00:21:35,319 --> 00:21:36,160
I need to ask you.

324
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:37,360
Okay.

325
00:21:38,559 --> 00:21:39,880
That boy from school...

326
00:21:40,559 --> 00:21:41,440
What's with you two?

327
00:21:42,799 --> 00:21:43,519
Him?

328
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,000
He's just

329
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,839
someone I rehearse with.

330
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,720
I didn't ask who he was.

331
00:21:49,079 --> 00:21:50,440
I asked what happened.

332
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:51,720
He was just...

333
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:54,440
He was asking me something.

334
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:57,400
Why won't you answer me?

335
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,119
What really happened between you?

336
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,799
Why was he grabbing you?

337
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,240
It was about our school's

338
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:03,400
English recitation team.

339
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:05,759
He was probably just anxious

340
00:22:05,759 --> 00:22:07,359
and grabbed me.

341
00:22:07,799 --> 00:22:08,720
It's fine, Mom.

342
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:09,880
Don't worry.

343
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:11,680
Good, you're okay.

344
00:22:12,759 --> 00:22:13,599
That's what matters.

345
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:14,799
Okay.

346
00:22:16,799 --> 00:22:18,000
Why are you dodging me?

347
00:22:18,519 --> 00:22:19,240
What?

348
00:22:19,559 --> 00:22:20,279
Why so nervous?

349
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:23,799
What's that?

350
00:22:24,839 --> 00:22:26,839
I just washed something.

351
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,759
I'll go hang it up.

352
00:22:28,799 --> 00:22:30,200
Give it to me.

353
00:22:30,319 --> 00:22:30,839
Stop.

354
00:22:30,839 --> 00:22:31,440
Don't touch it.

355
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,519
I always wash your clothes.

356
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:36,680
What got into you today?

357
00:22:36,799 --> 00:22:37,799
I need it tomorrow.

358
00:22:37,799 --> 00:22:39,079
Why wash it yourself

359
00:22:39,079 --> 00:22:40,000
this late at night?

360
00:22:40,079 --> 00:22:41,039
What happened to them?

361
00:22:41,079 --> 00:22:41,880
What happened?

362
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:42,400
Nothing.

363
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:43,079
Then what?

364
00:22:48,599 --> 00:22:50,640
I fell today.

365
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:54,119
It only tore a little.

366
00:22:54,759 --> 00:22:56,000
I didn't want you to worry

367
00:22:57,079 --> 00:22:59,359
or scold me, so I washed it myself.

368
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:00,599
If your uniform tore,

369
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,200
I could've stitched it.

370
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:04,359
Don't hide things from me.

371
00:23:04,839 --> 00:23:06,640
You need to tell me things yourself.

372
00:23:06,759 --> 00:23:08,119
You hide everything,

373
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:09,400
and when I find out later,

374
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:11,480
I get furious.

375
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,359
Try to understand how I feel,

376
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:14,160
okay?

377
00:23:14,519 --> 00:23:16,400
I understand, Mom.

378
00:23:17,279 --> 00:23:18,759
I'll tell you from now on, okay?

379
00:23:19,359 --> 00:23:20,799
Tell me everything.

380
00:23:27,640 --> 00:23:28,359
Drink your milk.

381
00:23:29,039 --> 00:23:30,079
- Rinse after.
- Okay.

382
00:23:31,119 --> 00:23:32,200
I'll stitch it up later.

383
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,079
Okay.

384
00:23:33,119 --> 00:23:34,480
Get some sleep too, Mom.

385
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:52,440
Director Hu.

386
00:23:57,519 --> 00:23:58,599
Up all night again?

387
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,279
That Wang...

388
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:03,720
Going to Municipal No. 2 Prison?

389
00:24:04,039 --> 00:24:04,400
Yes.

390
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,079
Your letter is ready.

391
00:24:09,839 --> 00:24:10,960
Take care of yourself.

392
00:24:11,079 --> 00:24:11,680
Get some rest.

393
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:12,559
I...

394
00:24:13,799 --> 00:24:14,960
Thank you, Director Hu.

395
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:23,599
Ting!

396
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:24,480
Ting!

397
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:25,400
Over here!

398
00:24:26,319 --> 00:24:26,759
Dad.

399
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:27,440
Ting.

400
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:29,839
Ting.

401
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:31,920
At lunch,

402
00:24:32,119 --> 00:24:33,039
come out early.

403
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:34,200
Roast duck for lunch?

404
00:24:34,359 --> 00:24:35,519
Your favorite. Okay?

405
00:24:35,519 --> 00:24:37,119
I have to eat with Mom.

406
00:24:37,359 --> 00:24:38,640
No need. It's fine.

407
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:39,240
Here.

408
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:39,880
Come on.

409
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:40,359
Sun Weiming!

410
00:24:40,559 --> 00:24:40,920
Mom.

411
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:41,400
What are you doing?

412
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:42,400
What?

413
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,759
I'm seeing my daughter.

414
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:46,519
You've been gone for years.

415
00:24:47,039 --> 00:24:48,839
When did you care how we felt?

416
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:50,079
Now you're back,

417
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:51,920
you keep coming to see Ting.

418
00:24:52,799 --> 00:24:53,759
You sneak behind my back

419
00:24:54,119 --> 00:24:55,240
and see her at school.

420
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:56,440
What are you after?

421
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:57,599
What could I be after?

422
00:24:57,759 --> 00:24:58,559
She's my daughter.

423
00:24:58,559 --> 00:24:59,319
I'm her father.

424
00:24:59,759 --> 00:25:01,240
A father has every right to see her.

425
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:02,759
The law protects that right.

426
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:03,599
Don't be absurd.

427
00:25:03,599 --> 00:25:04,039
Watch it.

428
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:04,799
Come on, Ting.

429
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:05,319
Come on.

430
00:25:05,319 --> 00:25:06,160
Don't grab her!

431
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:06,799
What?

432
00:25:06,799 --> 00:25:08,160
She's not your property.

433
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:09,240
What did I do?

434
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:11,480
Who are you?

435
00:25:12,079 --> 00:25:12,720
What are you doing?

436
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:14,000
A grown man like you

437
00:25:14,279 --> 00:25:15,680
putting hands on a woman?

438
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:16,720
Why wouldn't it be?

439
00:25:17,039 --> 00:25:18,039
None of your business.

440
00:25:18,119 --> 00:25:19,200
It's a family matter.

441
00:25:19,359 --> 00:25:20,119
What's it to you?

442
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:21,839
We have nothing to do with him.

443
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,039
Say that again.

444
00:25:23,039 --> 00:25:23,640
Get lost!

445
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:24,960
She's my daughter!

446
00:25:25,039 --> 00:25:25,640
Call the cops.

447
00:25:25,799 --> 00:25:26,359
Call them.

448
00:25:28,079 --> 00:25:28,440
Fine.

449
00:25:29,119 --> 00:25:30,000
Then call them.

450
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:31,599
Fine.

451
00:25:31,799 --> 00:25:33,000
You're a factory official.

452
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,680
Getting too comfortable there?

453
00:25:35,079 --> 00:25:35,480
Fine.

454
00:25:36,039 --> 00:25:37,160
Let's make a scene

455
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,480
and see if you keep your post.

456
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:40,440
A factory official?

457
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:41,160
That's right.

458
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:42,319
An official.

459
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,079
Even easier.

460
00:25:43,599 --> 00:25:44,119
Get the cops.

461
00:25:44,519 --> 00:25:45,200
I'll testify.

462
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:46,799
There's a phone here.

463
00:25:46,839 --> 00:25:47,960
Should I call, or will you?

464
00:25:48,440 --> 00:25:48,839
Ting.

465
00:25:49,519 --> 00:25:49,960
Look.

466
00:25:50,319 --> 00:25:51,160
We'll meet another day

467
00:25:51,440 --> 00:25:52,160
and have lunch.

468
00:25:56,960 --> 00:25:57,880
All right. It's over.

469
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:58,519
It's okay.

470
00:25:59,079 --> 00:25:59,559
It's okay.

471
00:26:00,319 --> 00:26:01,400
Back to school, kids.

472
00:26:06,759 --> 00:26:07,519
Go home.

473
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,039
Ting, I'll come another day.

474
00:26:15,079 --> 00:26:15,799
I'm sorry.

475
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:16,839
Sorry for the trouble.

476
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:17,519
Not at all.

477
00:26:17,759 --> 00:26:18,240
Thank you.

478
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:18,880
Not at all.

479
00:26:20,559 --> 00:26:20,960
Come on.

480
00:26:24,279 --> 00:26:24,759
Miss?

481
00:26:26,119 --> 00:26:27,240
Could I have a moment?

482
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:28,480
I wanted to ask...

483
00:26:29,039 --> 00:26:29,960
Do you know a student

484
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:30,920
named Su Lin?

485
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:33,160
(Mind your own business.)

486
00:26:33,799 --> 00:26:34,880
(Eat it.)

487
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,079
(Why'd you butt in?)

488
00:26:37,079 --> 00:26:38,599
(I told you to stay out of it.)

489
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:40,799
You do?

490
00:26:42,160 --> 00:26:42,880
No, I don't.

491
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:44,440
Ting!

492
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:45,039
Ting!

493
00:26:45,319 --> 00:26:45,720
Ting!

494
00:26:45,839 --> 00:26:46,759
Sorry.

495
00:26:47,279 --> 00:26:48,720
She's late for school.

496
00:26:49,039 --> 00:26:49,519
Thank you.

497
00:26:49,799 --> 00:26:50,880
Ting! Come on.

498
00:26:51,519 --> 00:26:52,759
I'll pick you up later.

499
00:26:55,119 --> 00:26:55,880
We don't have

500
00:26:56,079 --> 00:26:57,920
any serial killers here.

501
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,920
Just one serial rapist.

502
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:02,720
The one from Nanjiang?

503
00:27:03,079 --> 00:27:03,400
Yes.

504
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:04,799
He

505
00:27:05,039 --> 00:27:06,359
didn't have the nerve to kill.

506
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:10,880
Was there a pattern to his crimes?

507
00:27:11,359 --> 00:27:13,319
He struck after fights with his wife.

508
00:27:14,359 --> 00:27:16,519
Many rapists are like that.

509
00:27:16,920 --> 00:27:18,279
They feel unfulfilled,

510
00:27:18,519 --> 00:27:19,559
so they offend.

511
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,279
How was he caught?

512
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:22,720
He got too brazen.

513
00:27:23,079 --> 00:27:24,279
When he attacked,

514
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:25,720
he started giving his own name.

515
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:28,359
Of course he got caught.

516
00:27:32,119 --> 00:27:32,599
All right.

517
00:27:33,119 --> 00:27:33,839
I understand.

518
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:35,680
Dinner's on me next time.

519
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:36,279
Sure.

520
00:27:36,640 --> 00:27:38,559
I won't keep you any longer.

521
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:39,640
I heard there's a

522
00:27:39,640 --> 00:27:40,720
criminal psychology professor.

523
00:27:41,039 --> 00:27:41,839
Could you introduce us?

524
00:27:42,039 --> 00:27:43,720
Young man, you wanted me?

525
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:45,079
Well.

526
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:46,480
Let me introduce you.

527
00:27:47,079 --> 00:27:49,319
This professor is conducting research

528
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:50,720
on criminal psychology here.

529
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:51,519
Professor Qiao.

530
00:27:52,559 --> 00:27:54,440
This is Tai Wei from Major Crimes.

531
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:55,920
Hello, Professor.

532
00:27:55,920 --> 00:27:56,680
- Hello.
- I'm honored.

533
00:27:56,839 --> 00:27:57,799
I've heard about you.

534
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:00,640
Know the Weihong Canal case?

535
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:01,519
Straight to it?

536
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:03,480
Not even a little small talk

537
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:05,119
before putting me to work?

538
00:28:05,160 --> 00:28:06,119
We don't have a choice.

539
00:28:06,359 --> 00:28:07,200
Every second counts.

540
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:12,640
Nice shot.

541
00:28:13,559 --> 00:28:14,039
Professor.

542
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:15,599
- About the case...
- Keep going.

543
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:16,720
Make it tough.

544
00:28:22,720 --> 00:28:23,839
Why

545
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:26,640
did you hit the five ball first?

546
00:28:27,119 --> 00:28:28,839
(Xinmin Billiards Hall)
Both were close.

547
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:29,799
It was an easy shot.

548
00:28:32,680 --> 00:28:34,240
What about those last two?

549
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:35,240
Same reason.

550
00:28:35,319 --> 00:28:37,119
I knew I could make them.

551
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:38,680
The killer chose his victims

552
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:40,839
using the same logic.

553
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:42,279
You mean

554
00:28:42,880 --> 00:28:45,000
he also chose targets

555
00:28:45,599 --> 00:28:46,359
he felt sure about?

556
00:28:46,799 --> 00:28:49,039
Not the targets.

557
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:52,599
He felt sure about the area.

558
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:53,440
In other words,

559
00:28:53,559 --> 00:28:55,799
it was a relatively

560
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:57,000
safe

561
00:28:57,200 --> 00:28:59,039
and stable area for him.

562
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:01,519
How do we define its boundaries?

563
00:29:02,759 --> 00:29:04,359
Serial crimes follow a pattern.

564
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:06,319
During a killer's first offense,

565
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:08,640
he's anxious and inexperienced.

566
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:09,960
So he'll likely

567
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:11,799
strike somewhere familiar.

568
00:29:18,599 --> 00:29:20,680
Near home or work, for example.

569
00:29:21,279 --> 00:29:24,200
As he grows more skilled and confident,

570
00:29:24,519 --> 00:29:27,319
he'll venture into unfamiliar areas.

571
00:29:27,960 --> 00:29:30,400
So his hunting ground expands.

572
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:31,160
Right.

573
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:34,799
The pool table is only

574
00:29:34,799 --> 00:29:35,839
a rough analogy.

575
00:29:37,039 --> 00:29:38,279
The actual theory

576
00:29:38,559 --> 00:29:40,960
comes from American psychologist Canter.

577
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:42,400
The circle hypothesis.

578
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:45,119
For a series of crimes,

579
00:29:45,519 --> 00:29:47,799
connect the two farthest crime scenes

580
00:29:48,119 --> 00:29:49,160
with a line.

581
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:50,359
Use that line

582
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:51,559
as the diameter

583
00:29:52,079 --> 00:29:53,559
to draw a circle containing

584
00:29:53,599 --> 00:29:55,279
(Killer's Comfort Zone)
every crime scene.

585
00:29:57,880 --> 00:29:59,200
Under the circle hypothesis,

586
00:29:59,400 --> 00:30:00,400
the offender

587
00:30:00,640 --> 00:30:02,359
lives within that circle,

588
00:30:02,759 --> 00:30:03,960
most likely

589
00:30:05,039 --> 00:30:08,039
near its center.

590
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:11,799
(Killer's Comfort Zone
Suspect's Base)

591
00:30:11,799 --> 00:30:13,839
How can you tell?

592
00:30:14,440 --> 00:30:15,519
On his first offense,

593
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:16,839
a suspect

594
00:30:17,119 --> 00:30:18,319
won't choose

595
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:19,920
somewhere too close to home.

596
00:30:20,559 --> 00:30:22,640
The risk of exposure is too high.

597
00:30:23,839 --> 00:30:24,960
The distance from his home

598
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:25,759
or workplace

599
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:27,920
to the first crime scene

600
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:30,039
is his safe distance.

601
00:30:31,599 --> 00:30:32,720
For his

602
00:30:32,720 --> 00:30:34,079
second offense,

603
00:30:34,720 --> 00:30:37,480
(First Crime Scene)
the first site is no longer safe.

604
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:40,079
He'll keep the same safe distance

605
00:30:40,319 --> 00:30:41,720
(Crime Scene 2)
then strikes elsewhere.

606
00:30:42,279 --> 00:30:42,880
I see.

607
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:44,200
Same distance, new direction.

608
00:30:44,359 --> 00:30:46,519
That forms the circle you described.

609
00:30:47,559 --> 00:30:48,640
One more question,

610
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:49,240
Professor Qiao.

611
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:52,279
We don't know where he lives.

612
00:30:52,319 --> 00:30:53,240
How can I determine

613
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,319
the approximate area

614
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:55,319
of that location?

615
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:57,160
That brings us

616
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:58,960
to another theory,

617
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:00,759
the buffer zone.

618
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:05,319
A buffer zone is where a killer

619
00:31:05,559 --> 00:31:07,119
will never commit a crime.

620
00:31:07,599 --> 00:31:10,559
It's usually too close to home.

621
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:12,359
He might meet someone he knows,

622
00:31:12,799 --> 00:31:14,920
increasing his risk of exposure.

623
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:17,200
If we identify the buffer zone,

624
00:31:17,359 --> 00:31:18,839
we can probably locate

625
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:21,079
the killer's home.

626
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:24,039
(Suspect's Base)

627
00:31:24,039 --> 00:31:24,920
You said

628
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:27,720
(Sun Hui First Crime Scene)
Sun Hui and Yang Xinqian

629
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:30,039
(Yang Xinqian Scene 2)
vanished farthest apart.

630
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:31,960
Those two points

631
00:31:32,200 --> 00:31:34,319
mark his maximum range.

632
00:31:35,119 --> 00:31:37,640
(Assumed Site Du Yuan)
She vanished closest to center.

633
00:31:37,759 --> 00:31:38,839
That's the key.

634
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:42,440
Use the distance from her location

635
00:31:42,519 --> 00:31:43,200
as the radius.

636
00:31:43,599 --> 00:31:45,000
(Suspect's Base)
Draw a small circle.

637
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:48,000
This smaller circular area

638
00:31:48,039 --> 00:31:50,799
is the killer's buffer zone.

639
00:31:53,240 --> 00:31:53,640
Professor,

640
00:31:53,640 --> 00:31:54,440
I'll draw it now.

641
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:55,960
Please tell me if it's right.

642
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:57,480
Clear table seven.

643
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:58,640
He's paying.

644
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:08,720
Today we'll study The Faults of Qin.

645
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:11,279
The author was a Western Han writer,

646
00:32:11,279 --> 00:32:11,880
Jia Yi.

647
00:32:12,559 --> 00:32:13,519
Here, the word

648
00:32:13,920 --> 00:32:14,960
is a verb.

649
00:32:15,519 --> 00:32:16,680
It means to criticize.

650
00:32:18,920 --> 00:32:20,920
So The Faults of Qin means

651
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:23,359
to point out Qin's failings.

652
00:32:27,119 --> 00:32:28,039
Excuse me.

653
00:32:28,519 --> 00:32:30,440
Class is in session. Who do you need?

654
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:32,400
I'm Jiang Ting's father.

655
00:32:32,599 --> 00:32:34,160
I need her for a family matter.

656
00:32:34,559 --> 00:32:35,680
May she miss one period?

657
00:32:36,400 --> 00:32:36,880
Jiang Ting.

658
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:38,400
Come here. Someone's here for you.

659
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:40,559
- Come.
- Get your bag.

660
00:32:42,640 --> 00:32:44,160
(New English Course)

661
00:32:44,400 --> 00:32:45,240
I've been waiting.

662
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:46,640
But then I thought,

663
00:32:47,039 --> 00:32:48,480
if I waited until school let out,

664
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:50,359
I'd run into your mom.

665
00:32:50,839 --> 00:32:52,200
So I came early.

666
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:54,880
Dad, is something wrong?

667
00:32:55,039 --> 00:32:56,359
You sound just like your mom.

668
00:32:56,759 --> 00:32:58,279
Can't I visit without a reason?

669
00:32:58,960 --> 00:32:59,599
Nothing major.

670
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:00,720
Today,

671
00:33:01,079 --> 00:33:02,119
I'm treating you.

672
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:03,519
Your favorite.

673
00:33:03,799 --> 00:33:04,359
A real treat.

674
00:33:04,519 --> 00:33:04,920
Come on.

675
00:33:05,079 --> 00:33:06,480
I have something else soon.

676
00:33:06,680 --> 00:33:08,200
This won't take long.

677
00:33:08,559 --> 00:33:08,960
Come on.

678
00:33:10,519 --> 00:33:11,440
Duck, two ways.

679
00:33:11,599 --> 00:33:12,480
Try the soup first.

680
00:33:13,160 --> 00:33:14,000
It's good.

681
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:15,279
Let me serve you some.

682
00:33:16,079 --> 00:33:17,559
I still have to eat at home.

683
00:33:18,839 --> 00:33:19,559
That's okay.

684
00:33:20,759 --> 00:33:22,000
You can eat your mom's cooking

685
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:23,200
anytime.

686
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,640
It's good to mix things up

687
00:33:25,680 --> 00:33:26,559
and eat well.

688
00:33:26,799 --> 00:33:28,119
Have some duck.

689
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:30,279
Some scallions.

690
00:33:30,480 --> 00:33:31,160
They're a must.

691
00:33:31,160 --> 00:33:31,920
I hate scallions.

692
00:33:34,799 --> 00:33:36,119
All right, no scallions.

693
00:33:36,279 --> 00:33:36,720
Here.

694
00:33:38,039 --> 00:33:39,279
When you were little,

695
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:41,559
whenever roast duck was on TV,

696
00:33:42,039 --> 00:33:43,359
your mouth would water.

697
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:47,640
Whenever you aced a test,

698
00:33:47,799 --> 00:33:49,240
you'd beg for roast duck.

699
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:50,759
You said you'd go to Beijing

700
00:33:51,359 --> 00:33:52,039
and eat it daily.

701
00:33:52,480 --> 00:33:53,279
You remember that?

702
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:54,880
Of course I do.

703
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:57,119
Eat up.

704
00:34:01,119 --> 00:34:01,720
Ting.

705
00:34:02,880 --> 00:34:04,039
Still want to go to Beijing?

706
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:06,359
I can take you with me.

707
00:34:10,039 --> 00:34:10,679
I

708
00:34:11,119 --> 00:34:12,480
was transferred there for work.

709
00:34:14,199 --> 00:34:14,880
Before now,

710
00:34:15,079 --> 00:34:16,320
I never had the chance

711
00:34:16,480 --> 00:34:17,760
to see how you were doing.

712
00:34:24,199 --> 00:34:25,519
I've looked into the college entrance

713
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:27,519
rules for vocational students.

714
00:34:28,159 --> 00:34:28,719
Run.

715
00:34:29,360 --> 00:34:29,920
Keep running.

716
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:30,559
Stay back!

717
00:34:31,159 --> 00:34:31,760
Stay back!

718
00:34:32,440 --> 00:34:33,159
(Go on, run.)

719
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:35,280
(There's nowhere left to go.)

720
00:34:35,679 --> 00:34:37,079
You can take the exam in Beijing.

721
00:34:38,079 --> 00:34:38,880
It'll be

722
00:34:38,920 --> 00:34:39,840
much easier there.

723
00:34:40,320 --> 00:34:41,400
(Where else can you run?)

724
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:44,360
How soon can we go?

725
00:34:46,719 --> 00:34:47,320
How soon?

726
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:49,840
How soon can we go to Beijing?

727
00:34:50,960 --> 00:34:51,880
The sooner, the better.

728
00:34:52,599 --> 00:34:53,199
Two months.

729
00:34:53,880 --> 00:34:54,639
Within two months,

730
00:34:54,800 --> 00:34:56,639
I'll have your schooling arranged.

731
00:34:56,960 --> 00:34:57,800
Okay. Two months.

732
00:35:00,400 --> 00:35:00,960
Ting,

733
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:02,880
don't worry.

734
00:35:03,519 --> 00:35:04,360
This time, my company

735
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:05,840
can secure Beijing residency for me.

736
00:35:06,239 --> 00:35:07,920
You'll be registered there too.

737
00:35:08,559 --> 00:35:09,320
I checked

738
00:35:09,599 --> 00:35:10,320
your grades.

739
00:35:10,719 --> 00:35:11,679
Getting in there

740
00:35:11,719 --> 00:35:13,280
would be a breeze for you.

741
00:35:14,079 --> 00:35:15,440
I can get into college here too.

742
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:16,639
Right.

743
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:17,880
Of course.

744
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:21,239
A smart girl like you

745
00:35:21,280 --> 00:35:22,360
could get in anywhere.

746
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:24,280
But

747
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:25,960
what I mean is,

748
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:27,000
if

749
00:35:27,280 --> 00:35:28,880
you take the exam in Beijing,

750
00:35:29,639 --> 00:35:31,760
you could get into a top university.

751
00:35:36,079 --> 00:35:36,519
Look.

752
00:35:37,719 --> 00:35:38,960
These are Beijing schools.

753
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:40,679
Let's check them out

754
00:35:40,880 --> 00:35:41,480
and learn more.

755
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:42,880
See if any appeal to you.

756
00:35:45,599 --> 00:35:46,119
Take a look.

757
00:35:49,440 --> 00:35:50,679
When you were little,

758
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:52,559
you wanted to be a reporter, right?

759
00:35:52,719 --> 00:35:55,159
So major in journalism.

760
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:57,079
You could carry a camera

761
00:35:58,079 --> 00:35:59,239
and travel while you work.

762
00:35:59,400 --> 00:36:00,119
Sounds good?

763
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:02,800
Your mom, honestly.

764
00:36:03,599 --> 00:36:05,000
Why let you study accounting

765
00:36:05,079 --> 00:36:06,199
at a vocational school?

766
00:36:07,199 --> 00:36:08,360
Why didn't she pull strings

767
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:09,360
and transfer you?

768
00:36:14,719 --> 00:36:15,199
Dad.

769
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:20,159
Do you know if I want to be

770
00:36:20,199 --> 00:36:21,079
a reporter or accountant?

771
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,039
A reporter, obviously.

772
00:36:23,559 --> 00:36:24,199
Accounting is just

773
00:36:24,199 --> 00:36:25,360
fiddling with an abacus

774
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:26,199
and keeping books.

775
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:27,000
How dull.

776
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:27,800
Right?

777
00:36:28,079 --> 00:36:29,159
It can't beat reporting.

778
00:36:29,960 --> 00:36:30,840
Here, eat.

779
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:32,639
Dad, I'm done.

780
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:34,960
I need to get back.

781
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:37,320
I have an accounting exam later.

782
00:36:38,360 --> 00:36:39,679
I want to place first

783
00:36:40,679 --> 00:36:41,800
and make Mom proud.

784
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:42,960
I'm going.

785
00:36:43,280 --> 00:36:43,719
Wait.

786
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:44,519
I'll take you.

787
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:45,599
No need.

788
00:36:46,159 --> 00:36:47,079
Just get back to work.

789
00:36:48,320 --> 00:36:49,519
There's a direct bus outside.

790
00:36:54,559 --> 00:36:55,119
Ting!

791
00:36:55,519 --> 00:36:56,000
Ting!

792
00:36:56,519 --> 00:36:56,960
Ting!

793
00:36:59,639 --> 00:37:00,119
Ting!

794
00:37:00,920 --> 00:37:02,360
Look at this booklet.

795
00:37:02,639 --> 00:37:03,000
(Admissions Guide)
Here.

796
00:37:03,840 --> 00:37:04,440
Take it.

797
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:06,320
Read it later.

798
00:37:07,039 --> 00:37:08,559
Don't worry about school in Beijing.

799
00:37:09,079 --> 00:37:11,239
I'll arrange it soon, okay?

800
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:15,199
I really need to go.

801
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:19,199
Let me walk you out.

802
00:37:19,559 --> 00:37:20,639
Sir, you haven't paid.

803
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:23,679
Pack it up, please.

804
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:02,320
Captain!

805
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:04,280
Let go. That hurts!

806
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:04,840
It hurts!

807
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:09,400
You kid.

808
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:11,480
Your reflexes aren't bad,

809
00:38:12,119 --> 00:38:13,199
but your moves need work.

810
00:38:14,119 --> 00:38:15,719
You hit way too hard.

811
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:16,480
Can't beat you.

812
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:18,400
If I were the killer,

813
00:38:19,079 --> 00:38:20,000
you'd already be dead.

814
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:21,360
Okay, okay.

815
00:38:22,039 --> 00:38:23,159
What brought you here?

816
00:38:23,639 --> 00:38:25,679
Remember the canvassing report

817
00:38:25,960 --> 00:38:27,400
on Du Yuan's last known whereabouts?

818
00:38:29,559 --> 00:38:30,599
Before leaving work,

819
00:38:30,719 --> 00:38:31,639
Du Yuan got a call.

820
00:38:31,920 --> 00:38:33,840
Her son wanted lamb buns.

821
00:38:34,159 --> 00:38:34,920
From this shop.

822
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,679
(Shengli Bun Shop)
We checked it.

823
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,679
The owner didn't remember her.

824
00:38:40,239 --> 00:38:41,920
Why come back now?

825
00:38:42,199 --> 00:38:43,559
At Municipal No. 2 Prison,

826
00:38:43,760 --> 00:38:45,880
I met Professor Qiao

827
00:38:46,199 --> 00:38:47,440
who explained a theory.

828
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:49,199
It can lead us to new clues

829
00:38:49,280 --> 00:38:50,320
from where Du Yuan vanished.

830
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:52,719
What theory?

831
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:53,920
Let's hear it.

832
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:55,480
Eat and talk.

833
00:40:56,400 --> 00:40:58,880
=Ren Yu=
(Next Time...)

834
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:03,520
(Su Lin)

835
00:41:10,599 --> 00:41:12,000
Aren't you looking for Su Lin?

836
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:12,920
Come on.

837
00:41:13,199 --> 00:41:14,159
I'll take you to her.

838
00:41:16,320 --> 00:41:16,800
Mom.

839
00:41:17,079 --> 00:41:18,159
If I went missing,

840
00:41:18,239 --> 00:41:19,239
would you look for me?

841
00:41:21,079 --> 00:41:22,079
Let go of me!

842
00:41:22,079 --> 00:41:22,800
You can't leave!

843
00:41:22,800 --> 00:41:23,440
Let go!

844
00:41:25,519 --> 00:41:27,960
Let me out!

845
00:41:28,280 --> 00:41:29,320
Let me out!

846
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:51,480
♪A faint heartbeat, scales drifting♪

847
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:57,640
♪In briny dark, scorched gills appear♪

848
00:41:58,120 --> 00:42:03,280
♪An empty shell, a banished soul♪

849
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:09,240
♪Moonlight splinters into shards♪

850
00:42:09,600 --> 00:42:15,400
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

851
00:42:15,640 --> 00:42:20,920
♪Dust drifts through the silent abyss♪

852
00:42:21,320 --> 00:42:27,040
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

853
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:33,800
♪Tides recede; we grow in the dark♪

854
00:42:57,200 --> 00:43:02,800
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

855
00:43:03,240 --> 00:43:08,640
♪Memories buried, sorrow forgotten♪

856
00:43:08,960 --> 00:43:14,280
♪Swim ahead, swim ahead♪

857
00:43:15,040 --> 00:43:21,780
♪Deep-sea wounds, we swim upstream♪

858
00:43:44,560 --> 00:43:50,160
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

859
00:43:50,900 --> 00:43:57,850
♪Deep-sea wounds, we swim upstream♪
